 "observations": [
  "col_left L1: the entry ecliptica of p. 385 goes on here.",
  "col_left L7, L8: the guillemets around «Gradus eclipticae in quo stella reperitur» are printed as small solid wedges, as on pp. 366, 370, 374, 377, 381, 382 and 384; «=» is printed long.",
  "col_left L9: the marks over both i of «al-Edrīsī» are bars (2.2-2.4 by 0.8-1.0 points), measured with macron_audit.py.",
  "col_left L16: the h of «Mizrāḥī» is the ḥ sort with its dot joined below; its first i is dotted, its last ī has a bar (2.4 by 1.1 points).",
  "col_left L17: «Ēliyyāh» has a macron over the capital E (4.1 by 1.1 points, at the height of the capitals); the ō of «Mōsheh» is the sort with its macron joined to the top of the o, as in Yōsēph (p. 380); «Bashyaṣī» has the dot under the s and a bar over the last i (2.4 by 1.0 points). The Hebrew «בשיצי» is unvowelled.",
  "col_left L19: the mark over the i of «al-Makīn» is a bar (2.3 by 1.0 points).",
  "col_left L20, L44: «ἔγκλισις τοῦ ἐκκέντρου, ἔγκλισις τοῦ ἐπικύκλου» and «ἐπίληψις» are Greek; their initial vowels carry the smooth breathing (with the acute in one sort in ἔγκλισις), as in ἄφεσις and ἀφέτης, p. 377.",
  "col_left L23: the italic ī of «*at-tadwīr*» has its bar.",
  "col_left L39: a stray upright mark (1.7 by 4.7 points) between «epicyclo-» and the column rule is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L3: «‘ērek» begins with the sign of ‘ayn and has a bar over the e (2.6 by 0.8 points). The Hebrew «עֵרֶךְ» is vowelled: ṣērē under the ‘ayin, sᵉgōl under the rēš, šᵉwā in the final kaf.",
  "col_right L4: the point after «(et add. 282)» is printed slanting (1.8 by 2.4 points) but stands on the baseline; transcribed as a point.",
  "col_right L6, L40: «ἔτος» and «οἰκειώσεις» are Greek: ἔτος with the smooth breathing and the acute in one sort, οἰκειώσεις with the smooth breathing over the ι and the acute on the ω.",
  "col_right L7: a round blot (3.5 by 3.7 points) above the line after «223 n.» is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L8: a speck in the margin before «Euclides» is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L13: a slanting stroke (3.7 by 1.7 points) after «{sc:xix}-{sc:xx}.», at the foot of the line, is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L23: the marks over the ā and the ī of «az-Zarqālī» are bars (3.2 by 0.8 and 2.0 by 1.0 points).",
  "col_right L32: a round speck (2.0 by 2.2 points) on the baseline far to the right of «planetarum.» is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L32, L33: a blank line separates the names in E from those in F.",
  "col_right L33: the first 2 of «299» is printed broken, its top apart from the rest.",
  "col_right L34: the d of «*faḍl*» has its dot below.",
  "col_right L36: the mark over the i of «ad-dīn» is a short bar (1.8 by 0.8 points), that of «ar-Rāzī» a bar (2.3 by 1.0).",
  "col_right L38: «*al-ḥūt*» has the dot under the h, «*al-ǵanūbī*» ǵ (Nallino's sign for jīm), a bar over the u and over the i (3.2-3.8 by 1.1-1.2 points); «α» is Greek.",
  "col_right L40: «Solis,» is printed heavier than the rest of the line (stems 1.6 points against 1.2-1.3); transcribed in the ordinary type.",
  "col_right L41: the z of «zodiaci» is printed broken, the end of its lower stroke apart from the letter.",
  "col_right L42: the 3 of «309» is printed broken, the end of its upper arm apart from the figure.",
  "col_right L43: «α» is Greek; «*al-fard*» has no dot under the d.",
  "col_right L44: «*al-mu’akhkhar*» has the sign of hamza after mu."
 ],
